    {
      "fact_id": "EXT016-generative-model-chunked-prefill-cannot-be-disabled-safely",
      "parameters": [
        "enable_chunked_prefill"
      ],
      "relation": "supported_domain",
      "question_types": ["supported_domain", "normalization_or_fallback"],
      "statement": "For a vLLM 0.20.0 generative model whose attention type is not encoder-decoder, is_chunked_prefill_supported resolves to true and EngineArgs enables chunked prefill by default. Explicitly disabling it is documented in the pinned implementation as not officially supported for such a generate runner and may crash the engine or produce incorrect outputs; false is therefore not a safe supported tuning value for that model class.",
      "applicability_when": [
        "vllm_version == 0.20.0",
        "runner_type == generate",
        "model attention type != encoder_decoder"
      ],
      "source_ids": [
        "vllm-model-config-source-0.20.0",
        "vllm-arg-utils-0.20.0"
      ],
      "source_locator": "ModelConfig.is_chunked_prefill_supported, lines 1702-1746; EngineArgs._set_default_chunked_prefill_and_prefix_caching_args, lines 2262-2284",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "fact_id": "EXT017-hybrid-kv-manager-has-no-distinct-qwen2-lmcache-path",
      "parameters": [
        "disable_hybrid_kv_cache_manager"
      ],
      "relation": "normalization_and_feature_gate",
      "question_types": [
        "activation_gate",
        "normalization_or_fallback",
        "supported_domain"
      ],
      "statement": "The vLLM 0.20.0 hybrid KV-cache manager distinguishes heterogeneous per-layer KV-cache specifications. For a model whose layers have one uniform full-attention specification, the group builder already takes the uniform path, so disabling the hybrid manager does not create a second layout. When kv_transfer_config is present, post-init disables HMA by default; explicitly enabling HMA is rejected if the connector lacks SupportsHMA. LMCacheConnectorV1 inherits KVConnectorBase_V1 but not SupportsHMA in the pinned source.",
      "applicability_when": [
        "vllm_version == 0.20.0",
        "model has a uniform full-attention KV-cache specification, or the active connector lacks SupportsHMA"
      ],
      "source_ids": [
        "vllm-global-config-source-0.20.0",
        "vllm-kv-cache-utils-source-0.20.0",
        "vllm-lmcache-connector-source-0.20.0",
        "vllm-kv-connector-factory-source-0.20.0"
      ],
      "source_locator": "VllmConfig post-init HMA rules around lines 1254-1319; get_kv_cache_groups around lines 1619-1630; LMCacheConnectorV1 declaration; KVConnectorFactory.create_connector HMA guard",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
